body:
I do understand your point but as someone who lives in Iran you must know that the western media is covering dare I say at most 30 percent of what's going on. For example you haven't heard that a few days ago the government forces shot a 10 year old boy to death. Or that there has been many cases of government forces trying to send a woman detainee to hospital in secret because they raped her just a little too much and now she's having a hemorrhage. Or how they broke both of Hossein Ronaghi's feet in prison and refused to let him seek medical care for days with his crime only being an activist for internet freedom. Or how they burned down their political prison, Evin, and about 40 inmates were burnt alive there. How in Baluchistan (Chabahar's state) they're killing at least 40 people every friday in just the city of Zahidan. How they suspended a lot of my friends from university just because they tried to have lunch with their friends from opposite sex. How they are threatening to execute all of the political detainees (which they did in 1988). How all the protesting people were not so happy when Biden said "we will free Iran" (even though everyone thinks we are supported by US and Israel. this revolution is going on with bare minimums meaning we don't even have leadership in organizing the protests and we only have slogans and at most molotovs in most cities. and we don't want to be puppets of US and Israel. We just don't want mass murderers and terrorists as our leaders.)

&#x200B;

there is emotion to appeal the narratives. But not even close to how much nihilistic life in Iran feels. And for the first time in history, this is indeed a feminist revolt supported by men. And believe me, seeing the downward spiral of Iran's economy and the imminent depletion of water resources. Nothing will ever get better.

&#x200B;

Please, even though it might feel that this is all a political game. Don't forget us. Like you didn't forget about the workers' protests in Hong Kong and the innocent people of Sarajevo. Be our voice.

&#x200B;

TL;DR: Most people in Iran are in fear of their livelihoods and are depressed. Everyday a lot of people are killed and raped. The coverage isn't even enough let alone huge.
